When we installing a bundler(parcel,webpack),a babel is installed as a dependency  with it  
Babel:
A babel is just a node package or library.Babel is just like another piece of js code which is reading our code and convert it to another code.It is just like a black box which is taking some code and splitting/throw out some code.The incoming code is the latest code of modern js version and outgoing js code is the older version of code.The conversion of new code to a old code is also known as POLYFill.

REACT.createElement
let heading=React.createElement('h1',{
id:'id1',key:'h1heading'},'Heading 1')
console.log(heading)
When we console it,we see that React.createElement returns an object,our react code convert that object to html code and show it in dom in this format
<h1 id='id1'>Heading 1</h1>

for multiple items,our REACT.createElement our code is very difficult to manage the code and difficult to read,thats why react gives us a JSX

JSX:
Jsx is a html like syntax but it is not html nor html inside JS

History of Jsx:
When fb created react,the major theory behind bringing react was that we want to do a lot of html and handle it with JS in a better way.SO they figure out that create a html element by React.createElement.Then it happened that for multiple elements creating using React.createElement,our code become very much messy and diffult to read & manage

Jsx example:
let heading=(<h1 id='id1'>Heading 1</h1>)  

JSX uses REACT.createElement behind the scenes,
babel convert Jsx code into REACT.createElement which returns an object and react convert that obj into html and show it on dom
JSX============================>React.createElement============================>Object====================================>HTML(DOM)
       babel converts                                  returns an object                 react convert it in html


Important:
U can also say (<h1 id='id1'>Heading 1</h1>) is a react element        
Benefits of JSX
1-Readability
2-Less code
3-Easy to Maintain
4-No Repitation
5-U can use Js & html like code together
