 Diff btw react element and react componnet
 
 React Element:
 React element is a normal variable which has assigned a some jsx.
 let heading=(<h1 id='id1'>Heading 1</h1>)  
 heading is a normal variable which is now known as react element because it is returning a Jsx which will convert in an object by babel,so we can also say that it is returning a object
Both the statements are true
 a)It is returning a Jsx   b)it is returning a object

Below is react component(As u see,its a proper function)
const heading=()=>{
return <h1>Kesa</h1>
}

So react element is object && react component is a function
--------------------
How to use react element in react component?

 let heading=(<h1 id='id1'>Heading 1</h1>)  
 
const headingComponent=()=>{
return (<>
<h1>Kesa</h1>
{heading}
</>)
}

How to use react component in another react component?

const headingComponent1=()=>{
return (<>
<h1>Kesa</h1>
{heading}
</>)
}

1st way:

const headingComponent2=()=>{
